  "name": "Cosmic death metal",
  "family": "rock_punk",
  "lineage": "Cosmic death metal is used here for the documented psychedelic/progressive death-metal field, with Blood Incantation’s Absolute Elsewhere as a selected branch. The record juxtaposes heavy guitar, fretless bass and drums with synthesizer textures. The band and producer describe extended ensemble preparation, drums tracked to tape then transferred to a DAW, and a Moog synthesizer beneath heavy sections. This authored five-role model emphasizes that metal/electronic contrast rather than treating the band’s wholly ambient Timewave Zero as death metal.",
